package storage

const submissionReviewSpecification = "Review the submitted work for task {source_task_id}: {source_title}. Read the parent comments, inspect the published changes, and verify the acceptance criteria. Evaluate YAGNI, DRY, and KISS. Do not edit the implementation. Use task_finish_review with approved when the submission can close, or changes_requested with concrete corrections the implementer must make. Put separately actionable discoveries in findings so amux can queue them as new tasks. Include your evidence in the review summary."

// Review instructions ported from the existing gateway templates.
const codeReviewSpecification = "Review the completed work for task {source_task_id}: {source_title}.\nRead that task and its associated comments for implementation and validation evidence. Inspect the actual changes. Follow repository instructions and KISS/YAGNI: report concrete introduced defects, not speculative enhancements or style preferences. Review only; do not implement changes. For confirmed actionable defects, check for duplicates and create normal queued finding tasks with concise evidence and suggested corrections. Post review results (including no findings) on the source task and this review task, then mark this review task done. Do not run the legacy reviews complete command. Completing this review does not create another review workflow."
const documentationReviewSpecification = "Review documentation pertaining to the completed change for task {source_task_id}: {source_title}.\nRead the source task, comments and actual implementation. Locate the affected user and agent documentation, examples, settings and platform requirements. Validate that documentation is updated correctly and matches the implementation; verify documented commands and behavior against the code. Follow repository instructions and KISS/YAGNI. Report concrete missing or incorrect documentation caused by this change, not unrelated rewrites. Review only; do not implement changes. Check for duplicate findings and create ordinary queued correction tasks under the source task with evidence and acceptance criteria. Post results (including no findings or no documentation affected, with a reason) on the source task and this review task, then mark this review task done. Completing this documentation review does not create another review."
